{"title":"2024 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2024 AMC 10B #5</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">2024 AMC 12B #5</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Simple_Algebra)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Simple Algebra)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the following expression, Melanie changed some of the plus signs to minus signs:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/0/a307bbc8aeccf32d5dea44474103639a57f21408.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1+3+5+7+...+97+99\\]\" width=\"219\" height=\"14\" />\nWhen the new expression was evaluated, it was negative. What is the least number of plus signs that Melanie could have changed to minus signs?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/6/a060897952f2b13e4fd9f15bb79f5f2d8a2c96f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 14 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 15 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 16 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 17 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"401\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Recall that the sum of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> odd numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/b/d6bd934594cbc77466175972cc386d99742a1c6d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 + 3 + 5 + 7+ \\dots + 97 + 99 = 50^2 = 2500.\\]\" width=\"339\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>If we want to minimize the number of sign flips to make the number negative, we must flip the signs corresponding to the values with largest absolute value. This will result in the inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/1/961b81f787fed7508b62c89c4db4a4f2830192c0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 + 3 + 5 +\\dots + (2n - 3) + (2n - 1) - (2n + 1) - (2n + 3)-\\dots - 97 - 99 &lt; 0.\\]\" width=\"537\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>The positive section of the sum will contribute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" />, and the negative section will contribute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/6/c464073e36d4d38028def94d64cc88d2d9cb2da5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-(2500-n^2) = (n^2 - 2500)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"222\" height=\"21\" />. The inequality simplifies to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/5/655fa59f1226d32b5ef977ba01acf5cd1ccfc154.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n^2 + (n^2 - 2500) &lt; 0\\]\" width=\"164\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/4/1d4e05f735e82749bfbfdeae464460bdf690064b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2n^2 &lt; 2500\\]\" width=\"86\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/4/3246341f0a640eda79a8fea455a652a3408e1542.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n^2 &lt; 1250\\]\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" />\nThe greatest positive value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> satisfying the inequality is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/6/6068ae8cde503d66da84a5ce7cba8bacfd7f9f39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />, corresponding to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7f6c79f2148f0cec592c9517b40ee1b82ef22e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> positive numbers, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/f/f4f7835f056fa214601a52cfe1d2a4841f1150c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{B. } 15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"53\" height=\"25\" /> negatives.\n</p><p>ALEX\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The formula for the sum of all odd positive integers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f9a96c63183be91b9fe70e6e16dfa4bfec6f3da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/d/b9d563064d7f949fd356a1c8e8e6a05a282f5319.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1+3+5+...+2n-3+2n-1=n^2.\\]\" width=\"301\" height=\"17\" />Therefore, the given sum evaluates to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3d63a68388f74a9d4e00d77159929d58dfd698.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[99=2(50)-1\\implies 50^2=2500.\\]\" width=\"253\" height=\"20\" /> Since we're looking for the minimum possible sign changes, we focus on the largest numbers in the set to change to negative.\n</p><p>If we change the sign of a number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> to negative, then the sum decreases by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f93f5c51ea4b04b4992b003b39479f29018f6bda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />. Therefore, we're looking for a subset of numbers that add to greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/c/bac5c75af96bae8044afb7783a94e56187bfbde8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2500/2=1250$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"117\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Now we look at the answer choices.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/c/e3c421240c815db03d17bec74e1cb3c8cac4aed6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) }14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" /> means that we're changing the signs of the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/0/1b0e54442061938743d0436400e04530ab4ea453.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{73,75,...,99\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"114\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/e/8fe3177fb369cb842b8a10c84122c6f81f963065.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$73+75+...+99=\\dfrac{(73+99)\\cdot(\\frac{99-73}{2}+1)}{2}=1204$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"399\" height=\"42\" />. \n</p><p>Now this so slightly happens to be less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/d/83d25f65c98ed0d9b4a0e798000d70071685d98b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1250$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/a/44a8e275f46b5aa591113def476d8fe7f34ccf0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(B) } 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> means we're adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/c/38c4bc29a5a0d6756b52b0277d9cd07e756225c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$71$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> to the set, too. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/7/7a7d001febc83407cd9721dcf7c732e3e790ffde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$71&gt;1250-1204=46$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"182\" height=\"15\" />, then the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/0/e70bc90b9fbcdf740e81f50c81c33def82f05fc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(B) }15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"62\" height=\"30\" /> ~Tacos_are_not_yummy_1\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that as mentioned above, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/b/42bfced5df3763e328a69400c8e14048386ff972.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 3 + 5... + 2n - 1 = n^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"205\" height=\"18\" />. So, the sum of the first 50 odd numbers is equal to 2500, and we need to find the smallest integer such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/f/31fe982bdb8c839193a7df4be68751f29cb1c1af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2k^{2} &lt; 50^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" />. Taking the square root, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/5/9653938a04cd89e96c147751f64a344fce9882f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 25\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"79\" height=\"21\" />, keeping in mind we need to take the floor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/1/d61ff234e56e50f5cb9fe5d35e5e8366d0f5a403.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2k^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"17\" /> needs to be slightly less than 2500. Using an approximation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/6/856b7929cd33f3b170ee674d6b8362d1f303d2c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2} = 1.4, 25 * \\frac{7}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"130\" height=\"38\" /> is 35, so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/0/e70bc90b9fbcdf740e81f50c81c33def82f05fc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(B) }15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"62\" height=\"30\" />\n~aleyang\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Simple_Algebra.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Simple_Algebra)\">Solution 4 (Simple Algebra)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Simple Algebra)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As mentioned above, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/b/42bfced5df3763e328a69400c8e14048386ff972.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 3 + 5... + 2n - 1 = n^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"205\" height=\"18\" />. This will be especially important in this solution. The sum of the original expression is 2500, so the combined (positive) sum of the negatives must be greater than half of this, i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/d/83d25f65c98ed0d9b4a0e798000d70071685d98b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1250$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />. We are looking to minimize the number of negative numbers, so we only convert the last numbers to negatives. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/a/b2a13ad3fe6a7f24282adc6eaf43fd0c897c6ec4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99 = o_1 = 100-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"143\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/7/357e0c13a6a2ca27b3c64c3388baa8497e3554ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$97 = o_2 = 100 - 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"143\" height=\"17\" />, and for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/a/89a9d4c42a2049616cba06b6a312715c38c9a097.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$o_n = 100-(2n-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"159\" height=\"20\" />. Then the sum of all numbers up till <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/a/99a90cf94ec083d2fe8065e89dea8b612a70d60c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$o_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/2/26238daf75cd6623c97b879266258176dfe6143e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100n - n^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" />. This sum needs to be greater than 1250, i.e.:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/8/5e856c38f2162592f4c93b34253ada805fdc6eaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100n-n^{2} &gt; 1250$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Testing out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> from the solution set yields the minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/c/21cee94ee92654e843d9cf2f18541e37eab00b47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />. The answer is therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/0/e70bc90b9fbcdf740e81f50c81c33def82f05fc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(B) }15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"62\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~mathwizard123123\n~ edit by RoyalPawn38\n</p><p>Video solution by Pi Academy\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/DIl3rLQQkQQ?feature=shared\">https://youtu.be/DIl3rLQQkQQ?feature=shared</a>\n</p><p>~ Pi Academy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 2 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=24EZaeAThuE\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=24EZaeAThuE</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/rZX4qVEflNg\">https://youtu.be/rZX4qVEflNg</a>\n</p><p>~Thesmartgreekmathdude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/mpnm_r6D3-w?t=1013\">https://youtu.be/mpnm_r6D3-w?t=1013</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2>